            <ArticleTitle>Ultrasound-guided caudad epidural access for the lumbosacral neurostimulation: case report and technical note.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-71; discussion 71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1525-1403.2010.00297.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This is a case report and description of a new ultrasound-guided caudad epidural needle placement for percutaneous stimulation of the lumbosacral roots.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Using ultrasonography pertinent spinal and neuroaxial anatomy was visualized. In-plane approach with continuous monitoring of the needle advancement was utilized. The needle was seamlessly placed in the epidural space on the first attempt.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Spinal sonography is a promising imaging method to facilitate percutaneous caudad epidural access.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2010 International Neuromodulation Society.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
